say performed on this patient uses fluorescence in situ hybridization   FISH  on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimens to analyze  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene  amplification status  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  dual color FISH assay was performed using Bacterial Artificial Chromosome probe  CTD  REMOVED_CASE_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   chromosome 8p   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus  home brew  and a copy number probe   centromere 8  Abbott Vysis 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  or 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       Signal quantitation was used to generate a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 8 ratio   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  Centromere 8 ratios are interpreted as follows  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered  borderline for amplification  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification   and greater than REMOVED_DATE or clustered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  signals that are too numerous to count  would be considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     REFERENCES   1  Turner N and Grose R  Fibroblast growth factor signaling  from  development to cancer  Nature Reviews Cancer 10 116   REMOVED_CASE_ID     2  Weiss J  Sos  M  et al  Frequent and focal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  amplification  associates with therapeutically tractable  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  dependency in squamous cell lung  cancer  Sci Transl Med 2 62  62ra93   REMOVED_CASE_ID       This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Jochen K Lennerz MD  PHD         PART   Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        report_end  , Suspicious.
