Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY IES   Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   RIGHT BREAST  UPPER INNER  11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A MASS  WITH CALCIFICATIONS   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  moderately differentiated  modified Bloom Richardson  grade II III   measuring at least 0 7cm in size   CARCINOMA IN SITU  solid type  intermediate nuclear grade  with central  necrosis and calcifications   Note  Both the invasive and in situ carcinoma consist of discohesive  cells and appear  lobular  in type  However  the presence of necrosis in  the CIS would be more typical of ductal carcinoma in situ   Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu will be performed and reported in an addendum   SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  blocks 1 and 2    Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   SEE NOTE  Note  The carcinoma appears to have prominent but grainy membrane  immunoreactivity for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  Given the  lobular  type morphology of the  tumor  this may represent edge artifact rather than true overexpression   Additional studies by FISH are suggested if clinically warrented   Interpretation   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  invasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but  only a portion of the membrane is positive   Positive  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells   Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity  in  10  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 68 year old female with RUI 6mm pleomorphic calcifications  associated with a density   Operation  11g stereotactic breast core biopsy  Clinical Diagnosis  R O invasive cancer  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Right stereotactic core biopsy  2 green cassettes    A  with  calcifications and  B  no calcification   GROSS DESCRIPTION  by SHAH RAJSHRI N  M D   The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit  number  and  right breast   and consists of two  2  light green cassettes  One  cassette is labeled  A  with calcifications and contains multiple  soft   fragmented  yellow to pink tissue cores  1 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate    The other cassette is labeled  B  and contains similar tissue fragments  2 5 x  1 5 x 0 4cm in aggregate    Micro 1   A   multi frags  ESS   Micro 2   B   multi frags  ESS   jks  Reports to  LEUNG  JESSICA  WAI M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY IES    report_end  , No.
