Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  HER 2 FISH  Non Breast  Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  L   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  71   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 8  YAWKEY 8 INFUSION  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 11 09  Results To   Jill N Allen MD      CLINICAL HISTORY   Gastrointestinal Tract  Pancreas  Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block s  from Massachusetts General Hospital  the archived specimen was  retrieved and reviewed for adequacy    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID             TEST    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Gastrointestinal Tract  Pancreas  Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     RESULTS      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number analysis      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION     The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene     TEST INFORMATION   Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  using formalin fixed paraffin embedded  tumor specimens was used to analyze  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene amplification status  Briefly   5 micron sections of formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor material were  prepared and an H E section reviewed to select regions for hybridization that  contain a majority of tumor cells  A dual color FISH assay was performed using  the PathVysion assay  Abbott Molecular  using a probe specific to the chromosome  17q  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus and a copy number control probe recognizing centromere 17  Signal  quantitation was used to generate a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 17 ratio  A ratio of   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 17 of REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered borderline for amplification  A  ratio between REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification  A ratio greater  than REMOVED_DATE or clustered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  signals that are too numerous to count would be  considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Miguel N Rivera MD         PART   Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        report_end  , Yes.
