Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 AUG 96 at 08 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO WITHIN O 05 CM OF THE ANTERIOR  SUPERFICIAL  MARGIN  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS APART FROM THE MAIN TUMOR  MINOR FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND RARE MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The tumor is separated from the anterior margin by a narrow plane of fibrous tissue  but appears to be completely excised  The tumor is about 1 0cm from the other margins  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 96 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  short suture equals superior  long suture equals lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan fibrofatty tissue  with orientation sutures as noted  The specimen is inked in black and anterior half double inked in yellow  It is sectioned to reveal a firm irregular stellate white mass about 1 8cm in diameter that extends to 0 2cm from the nearest margin  anterior   and about 1 0cm to the other resection margin  superior  inferior  lateral  medial and deep   Section Code  A  nodule with closest resection margin  B  nodule with superior resection margin  C  nodule with inferior resection margin  D  nodule with deep resection margin  E  lateral breast  uninvolved  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary node  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of red yellow fibroadipose tissue with severeal suture ligatures  No discrete mass is palpable  Seven lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm are isolated from the specimen bissected and entirely submitted in F through H  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  CLOSEST MARGIN ANTERIOR  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURC