eptor  Positive 161 fm mg cytosolic protein  progesterone receptor  Positive  REMOVED_CASE_ID  fm mg cytosolic protein  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section laboratory  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm REMOVED_DATE x 1cm white gray  gritty nodule  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in A  Representative sections are saved for BRDU and ER studies  The remaining non frozen tissue is submitted entirely in B I  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST NODULE  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 24 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  PRESENT IN SIX OF SIX SLIDES AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Ductal carcinoma in situ is identified in regions of tissue away from the main tumor mass  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue fragment inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm  ill defined stellate nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  extending grossly to an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  with two representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma in cassettes E and F  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA PRESENT AT MARGIN  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , No.
